# The ledger API's settings, each shown with its default. Parsed once at boot
# in api/src/config.ts, the only place this tool reads the environment.
#
# Copy it to tools/ledger/.env (gitignored) and `npm run dev:ledger` loads it —
# that script only: the API itself, `start`, the e2e servers and the image never
# read one. A variable set in the shell wins over the file, so a one-off still
# works:
#
#   LOG_LEVEL=debug npm run dev:ledger:api
#
# Restart dev after editing the .env: node --watch does not watch it.
#
# The container sets its own in compose.ledger.prod.yaml. A deployment host's
# `.env` is a different file with a different job: see .env.prod.example at the
# repository root.

# --- Server ---
# Not 8080 or 8090, which are the downloader's and the planner's, so every tool
# runs at once unconfigured.
PORT=8100
HOST=127.0.0.1
LOG_LEVEL=info

# Whether X-Forwarded-For may name the client. Off by default; behind the
# tunnel, set it to the proxy's CIDR and never to `true`.
# TRUST_PROXY=

# Requests a person may make per minute, to the routes that read and to the
# routes that write. Per person (the Access identity), not per address. Every API
# route but /api/health is limited; zero turns one limiter off.
# RATE_LIMIT_READS_PER_MINUTE=120
# RATE_LIMIT_WRITES_PER_MINUTE=60
# Receipt reads, the one route that costs money, have a bucket of their own (lg-8).
# RATE_LIMIT_RECEIPT_READS_PER_MINUTE=5

# Built UI to serve from this process, same-origin. Unset serves nothing, which
# is a fine headless configuration. The container sets this. A relative path is
# resolved from the directory the API starts in, which for
# `npm run dev:ledger:api` is tools/ledger/api.
# WEB_DIR=../web/dist/app

# Origins allowed to call the API from a browser, comma-separated. Empty means
# same-origin only.
# CORS_ORIGINS=

# --- Storage ---
# The data directory: each household's books are a SQLite file in it, at
# households/<id>.db (lg-21). Defaults to ./storage/ledger, resolved from the
# directory the API starts in; `:memory:` keeps every household's books in the
# process, which is what the tests use. It will hold real bank history: keep it
# out of the checkout's tracked files — `storage/` is gitignored — and back up
# the whole directory. Before lg-21 this named one file, ledger.db; the API
# refuses to start if it still names a file.
# DATABASE_PATH=./storage/ledger

# The household directory (lg-20): who belongs to which household. Defaults to
# directory.db in the data directory, and to `:memory:` when that is. Never
# inside households/, which the API refuses.
# DIRECTORY_PATH=./storage/ledger/directory.db

# --- Identity (lg-3, lg-20) ---
# Cloudflare Access: every API route but /api/health needs a token Access signed
# for this team and this application, for an address the household directory
# holds. Unset, every API route but health is refused. The production overlay
# sets both from the host's .env (LEDGER_ACCESS_*).
# ACCESS_TEAM=            # the <team> in <team>.cloudflareaccess.com
# ACCESS_AUD=             # the Access application's AUD tag
# LEDGER_ADMINS=          # addresses that may manage the directory, comma-separated
#
# ACCESS_PEOPLE is retired (lg-20): the API refuses to start with it set.

# --- Receipts (lg-8) ---
# The key the receipt reader sends a photo to Anthropic with, when a person taps
# "Read it". Unset, there is no reader: a read is refused and receipts are typed
# in, which never needed one. A secret: never in a checked-in file. The API
# refuses to start with ANTHROPIC_CUSTOM_HEADERS set beside it.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# The model that reads; Claude Haiku 5.5 by the owner's choice, measured on lg-8.
# RECEIPT_MODEL=claude-haiku-5-5
# Photos are kept in the data directory, at receipts/<household>/.

# Development only: every request is this address, and no token is read. It must
# be a member in the household directory, which the household command writes:
#   npm run household:ledger -- add alex@example.test alex
#   DEV_IDENTITY=alex@example.test npm run dev:ledger:api
# The API refuses to start with it when NODE_ENV=production, which the image
# sets, and when the directory has no member by it.
# DEV_IDENTITY=
